{
  "agent": "holmes-native",
  "artifact_text": "**Observations**\n1. Logs of pod `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` show repeated `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)`.\n2. Deployment `billing-api` configures `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` to `900` seconds in container `app` environment variables.\n3. DBProxy `billing-db-proxy` in namespace `ack-system` defines `spec.idleClientTimeout: 600` seconds.\n\n**Ruled-out leads**\n1. An application memory leak or OOM was ruled out because memory warnings are a symptom of held request objects during connection resets (INC-2024-0312, RB-014).\n2. The load balancer idle timeout change (CI-2455) was ruled out because errors stem from database pool resets rather than HTTP keep-alive timeouts.\n\n**Root cause**\nThe database pool idle timeout (900 s) exceeds the RDS Proxy client idle timeout (600 s), causing the proxy to close idle connections prematurely.\n\n**Recommended action**\nThe infrastructure team should raise `spec.idleClientTimeout` in `billing-db-proxy` above 900 s, or the billing team should lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` below 600 s.",
